An unfinished task stays unfinished when a `[x]` appears later in its own
line.

Upstream cmark decides "checked" in tasklist.c with

    strstr(input, "[x]") || strstr(input, "[X]")

over the WHOLE line rather than the three bytes it just consumed, so

    - [ ] Ship it [x] today

came back as `- [x] Ship it \[x\] today`. The document then said a task was
finished that nobody ever finished, which a reader cannot tell from what
the author wrote.

Whether an item HAS a box still comes from cmark. Whether the box is TICKED
is read from the source: the box opens the item content, so the first
bracket pair on the line is the box and everything after it is prose. The
third and fourth items check the rule in both directions.
